<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rathore</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rathore Rajputs, Rathore dynasty, Rathores, Rathores of Marwar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rathores are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> clan of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, who ruled Marwar from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandore">Mandore</a> and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jodhpur">Jodhpur</a> from the 15th century. Branches founded the states of Bikaner, Kishangarh, Idar, Ratlam and many smaller principalities in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a>. Many Rathore princes served as commanders of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>, and their states lasted until 1947.</p></div>
